{
  "comment": [
    "Security review 2026-10, root cause A §4.1 / §8.5 (branch A5). Hand-authored; every blob produced by an INDEPENDENT oracle (@noble/ciphers XChaCha20-Poly1305 + Node SHA-256, no libsodium, no andvari code) with fixed nonces.",
    "wrap: AccountKeys.personalWrap = Envelope(UVK, VK, Ad.vkPersonal(vaultId, userId)) with AD 'andvari/v1|vk-personal|{vaultId}|{userId}'. open rows MUST yield vkB64; reject rows MUST fail (cross-purpose: a personal wrap never opens as an owner wrap and the reverse; wrong vault; wrong user).",
    "migration: the §8.5 QUESTION as amended by the A5 review (H-1). There is NO automatic pick and the server label (labelledPersonal, kept in the rows only to prove it is ignored) neither filters nor orders: the choices are every candidate with ownUvkWrap (a key from a UVK wrap on our own grant row, no seal), the device's lastUsed first when it is one of them, then by vaultId. Rows never expect `auto`.",
    "decision (security review 2026-10, branch A11; c00, c01): the device's personal-vault decision table. Symbols: A = the vault enrolment made personal, C = an own-UVK shared vault, junk = a blob that does not open under the UVK, none = nothing. served = AccountKeys.personalWrap; cached = this device's durable cached wrap; designation = the account-state `personal.vaultId` (null = none); mergedStateBefore = the device had merged account state before this decision (a high-water mark). expected.status is the engine status; inForce is the personal vault in force ('' = none, no default destination); pending is the wrap waiting for the human (changed/proposed) or null. Rules pinned: a cached wrap is held as a PROPOSAL whenever the designation names another vault, whether the server served nothing, junk or a wrap (c00); a designation that moves AWAY from the cached vault is a CHANGED notice for the human, never a silent switch, merged state or not (c01: an intermediate genuine seq above the high-water mark is not a detectable rollback). The extension has no designation reader (spec 05 R14(e)) and runs only the designation-null rows."
  ],
